{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-21T11:59:13.788Z","data":{"text":"Task 2 complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the explicit rejection transition for change 036.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `src/core/layout.ts`: added `getRejectedDir` (`openspec/changes/rejected`).\n- `src/harness/types.ts`: added the typed `rejected` event + `RejectedEventData` to the discriminated union.\n- `src/core/reject.ts` (new): `rejectSpec` — validates a non-empty reason, resolves only active changes, refuses collision, inspects running markers and approval directly, and permits either an unapproved change or an approved change whose derived status is `dead`/`regressed` (active numeric/`change.md` markers only). On success it does one `fs.rename` into `rejected/<folder>/`, then writes `.run/rejected.md` and appends one `rejected` event to `.run/events/change.jsonl` sharing one ISO timestamp.\n- `src/cli/reject.ts` (new) + `src/cli/index.ts`: registered `reject <id>` with required `--reason <text>` guarded by an `InvalidArgumentError` parser.\n\n**Tests**: `tests/reject.test.ts` (15 cases: reason validation, all eligibility/refusal classes, exact destination, collision, marker/event agreement, byte-level retention of proposal/tasks/delta/plan/events/results/markers) and 3 new cases in `tests/cli.test.ts`.\n\n**Deviation**: `appendHarnessEvent` was not reused because `src/core` cannot import `src/harness` per the import-graph test; the event is appended directly as `src/core/done.ts`/`retry.ts` already do.\n\n**Verification**: task verify passes (21/21); `pnpm verify` (tsc + full suite + lint) exits 0. Result written to `openspec/changes/036-dead-letter-retry-and-rejection/.run/results/2.md`."}}
